{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Open your eyes</b> — from sleep, for then you will be sated with bread. And observe the buyer, who says of the merchandise, \"Bad, bad,\" and disparages it, so that he can buy cheaply. And when he goes about himself with the merchandise, then he boasts and glorifies himself and says that he knows how to acquire a fine thing. And so it is in truth: there is much gold and pearls for one who has lips of knowledge, that he know the business of trade."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:49.505756618Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}